1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,595
Every service operation runs on handovers.

2
00:00:02,895 --> 00:00:06,047
A technician records a finding, and the shift changes.

3
00:00:06,347 --> 00:00:10,103
Managers chase answers across notes, calls and systems.

4
00:00:10,403 --> 00:00:15,183
Time is lost asking, searching and re-keying, not repairing vehicles.

5
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:17,890
And critical details slip between shifts.

6
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:21,518
This is where the Service Operations Agent comes in.

7
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:25,249
It turns every update into one live view of the floor.

8
00:00:25,549 --> 00:00:29,397
Right now, 12 vehicles are flagged as unsafe to release.

9
00:00:30,497 --> 00:00:34,391
Here is how it works. A technician speaks or types an update.

10
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:38,911
NVIDIA Riva transcribes it, and Nemotron extracts the facts.

11
00:00:39,211 --> 00:00:42,502
Code verifies every fact. Nothing is guessed.

12
00:00:42,802 --> 00:00:44,841
Each update joins an audit trail.

13
00:00:45,141 --> 00:00:50,059
Managers simply ask, and receive cited answers. Here it is, live.

14
00:00:51,159 --> 00:00:54,177
In the live system, a technician dictates an update.

15
00:00:54,477 --> 00:00:57,115
NVIDIA Riva turns the speech into text.

16
00:00:57,415 --> 00:01:01,777
Nemotron extracts the facts: the measurement and the specification.

17
00:01:02,677 --> 00:01:07,317
Code verifies it, and flags the repair order unsafe to release, instantly.

18
00:01:08,717 --> 00:01:11,918
Next, a manager asks the question that matters.

19
00:01:12,218 --> 00:01:15,093
Which vehicles cannot be released on safety grounds?

20
00:01:15,393 --> 00:01:21,327
13 vehicles, each one cited, in a tenth of a second, with no model call.

21
00:01:22,027 --> 00:01:26,658
Then an open question: has anyone seen a whistling noise on a Passat?

22
00:01:26,958 --> 00:01:31,590
Search, reranking and a cited answer, in seconds, on the same GPU.

23
00:01:32,390 --> 00:01:34,802
Unsafe vehicles surface immediately.

24
00:01:35,102 --> 00:01:37,557
Managers get answers in a tenth of a second.

25
00:01:37,857 --> 00:01:40,316
Every figure traces back to a real record.

26
00:01:40,616 --> 00:01:44,559
And one update feeds the record, the handover and the dashboard.

27
00:01:44,859 --> 00:01:50,243
The deployed architecture: three NVIDIA NIMs on one L40S.

28
00:01:50,943 --> 00:01:55,398
Riva handles speech. NeMo Guardrails stops unsafe requests.

29
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:59,688
NeMo Evaluator scores every release. That is the whole stack.

30
00:02:00,988 --> 00:02:06,643
Observability is built in: DCGM and the app's own metrics, live in Grafana.

31
00:02:07,243 --> 00:02:13,274
In summary: 12 of 32 unsafe vehicles flagged the moment an update is logged.

32
00:02:13,574 --> 00:02:18,494
Answers in a tenth of a second, every figure traced, all on one L40S.

33
00:02:18,794 --> 00:02:24,085
Fast. Grounded. Yours to run. That is the Service Operations Agent.

